cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MELVcore in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MELVcore: A Thermodynamic Governance Kernel for Multi-Agent AI Systems"
abstract: >
  MELVcore is an open-source governance kernel that monitors and resolves
  resource contention in multi-agent AI ecosystems using principles derived
  from the Modified Energetic Lotka-Volterra (MELV) framework. It implements
  a cooperation index (CI) calibrated to an empirically derived bifurcation
  threshold (i_critical = 0.9995 ± 0.029, R² = 0.9248), below which
  cooperative equilibria are thermodynamically inevitable. The platform
  includes a three-scalar epsilon decomposition, sigmoid quorum gate,
  Oxpecker thermodynamic recycling, and a sandbox certification engine.
